When you run Pex on this code, the generated test case includes a setup of the input `arrList` with initial values and an expected result `x` along with verification methods for each added method call, including methods for asserting the arrayList `Count`, `IndexOf`, and `LastIndexOf` results change as expected, and `Contains` method returns `true` after addition. 

This approach not only covers what the method is expected to do but also provides valuable information for debugging. This is one of the powerful features of Pex - a generation of tests that not only pass the assertions but also cover as much of the code as possible.

> *[Note: NUnit and Microsoft.Pex packages should be installed through your project's NuGet Package Manager.]*


